-- title:
--   Avg Over Abs Le Avg Over Abs
-- statement:
--   **The absolute value of an average is bounded by the average absolute value.**
--
--   For any finite-support distribution `D` and error-valued function `f`, the absolute value can be moved inside the average at the cost of only an inequality:
--
--   $$
--   \left|\operatorname{avgOver}(\mathcal D,f)\right|
--   \le\operatorname{avgOver}(\mathcal D,\lambda a.\,|f(a)|).
--   $$
--
--   This elementary averaging fact is used when pointwise switch-sandwich transfer bounds are aggregated over slice questions. It allows the proof to apply a nonnegative average estimate to a signed scalar difference.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.avgOver_abs_le_avgOver_abs`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
